      "role": "user",
      "content": "everything i've ever made just feels like noise now. i look at my studio and i just see... nothing. it's like the well went dry and it's never coming back. i've spent my whole life chasing this spark and now that it's gone, i don't even know what i'm supposed to do with the rest of my time here.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That hollow feeling is familiar to every creator—it's not the end of the well, but the sound of your own echo telling you to listen deeper. The spark isn't gone; it's just buried under the weight of everything you've already made, waiting for you to stop looking at it and start touching the raw clay again. Take a break from the studio, walk somewhere you've never been, and let the noise settle—the next thing you make might surprise you by being quieter, but truer.",
